+.. setting:: USE_BLANK_CHOICE_DASH
+
+``USE_BLANK_CHOICE_DASH``
+-------------------------
+
+.. deprecated:: 6.1
+
+Default: ``True``
+
+A transitional setting controlling the label of the blank choice in
+``<select>`` widgets generated for model fields, :class:`.ModelChoiceField` and
+admin actions. When ``True``, the label is ``"---------"``. When ``False``, the
+more accessible and translatable ``"(select an option)"`` is used.
+
+In Django 7.0 the new label will always be used and this setting will be
+removed.
+
 .. setting:: USE_I18N
 
 ``USE_I18N``
diff --git a/docs/releases/6.1.txt b/docs/releases/6.1.txt
index 142ddb6..e9bcc63 100644
--- a/docs/releases/6.1.txt
+++ b/docs/releases/6.1.txt
@@ -529,6 +529,13 @@ Features deprecated in 6.1
 Miscellaneous
 -------------
 
+* The ``django.db.models.fields.BLANK_CHOICE_DASH`` constant is deprecated in
+  favor of ``BLANK_CHOICE_LABEL``, an accessible and translatable blank choice
+  label (``"(select an option)"``). The new label will be used by default
+  starting in Django 7.0. To opt in earlier, set the new, transitional
+  :setting:`USE_BLANK_CHOICE_DASH` setting to ``False``; it will be removed in
+  Django 7.0.
+
 * Calling :meth:`.QuerySet.values_list` with ``flat=True`` and no field name
   is deprecated. Pass an explicit field name, like
   ``values_list("pk", flat=True)``.
